<title>USA: St. Paul Bancorp Inc Q3 net higher.</title>
<headline>St. Paul Bancorp Inc Q3 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third Quarter	     Nine Months</p>
<p> Interest income  $74,864     $69,828    $220,173    $208,453</p>
<p> Interest expense  43,467	41,180     127,327     121,226</p>
<p>Net interest income</p>
<p>			 31,397	28,648	92,846	87,227</p>
<p>Provision for loan</p>
<p>   losses		 500	   300	 1,500	 1,400</p>
<p>Net interest income after</p>
<p>provision for</p>
<p>   loan losses     30,897	28,348	91,346	85,827</p>
<p>Other operating income:</p>
<p>Income from real estate</p>
<p>  operations	    643	   909	 1,842	 2,069</p>
<p>Net gain on assets sold</p>
<p>			    132	    91	 1,423	   967</p>
<p>  Other income	8,142	 7,713	23,395	22,118</p>
<p>Total other</p>
<p>operating income</p>
<p>			  8,917	 8,713	26,660	25,154</p>
<p>SAIF recapitalization</p>
<p>			 21,000	    --	21,000	    --</p>
<p>Other operating</p>
<p>   expenses	  24,768	22,464	72,500	67,530</p>
<p>Total operating</p>
<p>     expenses	45,768	22,464	93,500	67,530</p>
<p>Loss from foreclosed</p>
<p>real estate operations</p>
<p>			     89	   312	 1,245	   968</p>
<p>Income (loss)</p>
<p>   before taxes   (6,043)	14,285	23,261	42,483</p>
<p>Provision for taxes</p>
<p>			(2,501)	 5,225	 7,860	15,391</p>
<p>Net income (loss) *</p>
<p>			(3,542)	 9,060	15,401	27,092</p>
<p>Shares outstanding</p>
<p>		   18,081,846  18,705,709  18,081,846  18,705,709</p>
<p>Earnings per share:</p>
<p>   Primary	   (0.20)	  0.46	  0.81	  1.39</p>
<p>   Fully diluted   (0.20)	  0.46	  0.80	  1.38</p>
<p>	  (Dollars in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>* Without the one-time SAIF recapitalization charge, net income would have been $10,360,000 or $0.55 a share for the third quarter of 1996 and $29,303,000 or $1.54 a share for the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>NOTE: St. Paul Bancorp Inc had assets of $4.28 billion at September 30, 1996.</p>
